# No staging or commits until asked

Do not stage or commit any file until the user explicitly says to.

- Do not run `git add`, `git commit`, `git commit --amend`, or any command that stages or records a commit.
- Do not stage a subset of files "to be helpful," and do not commit after finishing a task.
- Leave the working tree as it is. Editing files is fine; putting them in the index or in history is not.
- Stage or commit only after a direct request in the current message, such as "commit this" or "stage these files." A request to implement, fix, or save code is not that request.

```text
# Not allowed on your own
git add .
git commit -m "..."

# Allowed only after the user asks
git add lib/features/books/
git commit -m "..."
```
